First Timers:

Welcome to the exciting new world of VBBS. It's a revolutionary Bulletin
Board System. VBBS allows the user to do many things all at one time. He/She
could be downloading messages, uploading files, downloading files, 
conferencing with a couple of other people (assuming 3 line BBS), chatting
with the sysop and reading Feedback ALL at the same time!!!

Obviously the faster the modem, the more you benefit from this multitasking.

What you need to do first is to set up your environment to your liking.
VBBSMenu configures your system enough so you can get started. For additional
features I would encourage you to read the Help document for Term (select it
by selecting HELP FILES and then TERM).

You are given 3 screens to fill out. Each of these screens, except the
first, offers full context help files as well as a HELP button. The first
screen is void of help, because you need only type in your name in the USER
NAME area and your password in the USER PASSWORD area. Once you are
satisfied with both, select ACCEPT.

This will move you onto the second screen. You'll notice there is a lot
more information to fill in on this screen. Not to worry. If you get stuck,
just select the appropriate text to get help. For example, if I was having
problems figuring out what was meant by MESSAGE DIRectory, I would move my
mouse over top of the words MESSAGE DIR and press down on the left mouse
button. A window will pop up describing the function and offer an example.

You'll notice you can only select one BAUD rate. This is as it should be
so don't worry.
 
Once you're happy with the information you have typed in, then select
ACCEPT. You should now be at the third window. This one is just point
and click. It deals with the Width, Height and number of colours you
wish on your TERM custom screen. If you want TERM to open up on 
Workbench, then just select YES, if you wish to open TERM up in its
own screen, then select NO (the default is NO).

After this is all done, you now select ACCEPT to finally accept those
results.

You are now ready to start up TERM. Just single click on TERM and 
select a BBS you wish to call and you're running TERM. If a VBBS BBS
is set up in your area and there isn't a script setup for that BBS,
then you will need to ADD the script to the list. For help with this,
just access the help button in the Select BBS panel.

If you do not have TERM, READ, AGE & VBBSReader in the same directory as
VBBSMenu, you will get a message telling you to re:run VBBSInstall. I
would recommend you do this as it will set everything up for you and you
don't have to worry about it.

You have now entered the world of VBBS. I hope you enjoy yourself and I
hope the process was fairly easy for you. If you ran into ANY problems
with these instructions or with VBBSMenu, please don't hesitate to
call Ian Gunn @ (403) 293-7102 evenings. 

